  "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\frac{2y}{x}}}3xyz\\,dz]dA & ={\u222c}_{D}{[\\frac{3}{2}xy{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{\\frac{2y}{x}}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}\\frac{3}{2}xy({(\\sqrt{\\frac{2y}{x}})}^{2}-0)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}\\frac{3}{2}xy\\cdot \\frac{2y}{x}\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}3{y}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}3{y}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{x-1}^{x+1}3{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{x-1}^{x+1}3{y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{y}^{3}]_{y=x-1}^{y=x+1}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(x+1)^{3}-(x-1)^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}(x+1)^{4}-\\frac{1}{4}(x-1)^{4}]}_{x=1}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(81-16)-\\frac{1}{4}(1-0) \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
